From ba26929ae03bc2f7c9dc0e795fc14d79bdfe534c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 04:35:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Read a big playlist once per visit, not once per page

Each playlist_tracks_page request read and deserialised the whole playlist from the
provider cache (about 0.2 s of event loop per page for 5000 tracks, plus a DB read per
provider page), and the count sent with the first page read it once more. A refresh
fetched the playlist from the provider twice in parallel. Items are now kept in memory
for 90 s (two playlists at most), overlapping requests share one read, sorted and
filtered views are built once, and a playlist edit clears what was kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
